# 20. CRITICAL BUG PREVENTION — FLICKER AND Z-FIGHTING

The owner has repeatedly encountered blinking and disappearing surfaces.

This room must receive a dedicated rendering stability pass.

Possible causes include:

- Coplanar duplicate polygons.
- Duplicate floor surfaces.
- Overlapping wall panels.
- Incorrect trim placement.
- Screen-plane overlap.
- Shelf face overlap.
- Shadow acne.
- Depth precision issues.
- Transparent sorting.
- Texture shimmer.
- Incorrect object mounting.
- Cutaway logic.
- Repeated procedural geometry creation.

Diagnose the actual causes rather than assuming one universal problem.

## INSPECT

- Rug and floor.
- Floor plank seams.
- Sofa cushion layers.
- Armchair geometry.
- Wall trim.
- Window frames.
- Testing devices.
- Monitor displays.
- Checklist board.
- Wall signage.
- Server racks.
- Rack status lights.
- Shelves.
- Storage drawers.
- Plants.
- Lounge table.
- Equipment cases.

## FIXING RULES

- Prefer source geometry corrections.
- Remove verified duplicate surfaces.
- Separate intentional layered planes by a small appropriate depth.
- Use correct material transparency.
- Avoid uncontrolled material overlays.
- Fix shadow bias only if the artifact actually comes from shadows.
- Keep texture frequencies appropriate for viewing distance.

Do NOT:

- Disable global depthTest.
- Disable global depthWrite.
- Apply polygonOffset to everything.
- Make everything double-sided.
- Remove shadows globally.
- Modify every existing room's rendering profile.
- Hide broken meshes from one camera angle only.

Do not claim the room has zero flicker without testing.

The acceptance target is no reproducible known flicker under the defined camera test sweep.

